{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1512","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1512","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1512\",\"parent_revision\":\"67376ade67e40c5e81056cd1aa863223cc7016f395df0312f63ad433ce56d907\",\"root_revision\":\"67376ade67e40c5e81056cd1aa863223cc7016f395df0312f63ad433ce56d907\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nsam_update in sam_schema/server.py coerces all values from set_fields_json to str before writing. Integer fields (e.g., priority, divergence-notes) are silently converted to strings, corrupting task YAML. Any downstream code expecting an int field receives a string. This was identified during the P912 TaskBackend code review as a pre-existing bug exposed by the refactor.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nREFUTED \u2014 No `str()` coercion of field values exists in `sam_update`.\\n\\nEvidence:\\n- `server.py:560` \u2014 `raw_fields: Any = json.loads(set_fields_json)` \u2014 JSON decode preserves types (int stays int, str stays str)\\n- `server.py:563` \u2014 `cast(\\\"dict[str, str | int | list[str]]\\\", raw_fields)` \u2014 `cast()` is a type annotation hint only; it performs zero runtime conversion\\n- `server.py:570\u2013574` (task-level path) \u2014 `raw_fields = json.loads(set_fields_json)` is passed to `_validated_task_patch`\\n- `server.py:505\u2013507` \u2014 `_validated_task_patch` merges raw_fields into current task data and passes through `Task.model_validate(...)` \u2014 Pydantic validation preserves field types and runs field validators\\n\\nThe task-level path is actually the **correct** implementation: it routes values through Pydantic model validation (`Task.model_validate`) which enforces types per the schema. The plan-level path uses `cast()` without Pydantic validation \u2014 this is a missing guardrail, not a coercion bug.\\n\\n**Re-scoped issue**: The real gap is that plan-level `set_fields_json` values bypass Pydantic validation and are written directly after only a `isinstance(raw_fields, dict)` check. An int field passed as a string (`\\\"priority\\\": \\\"3\\\"`) would be accepted without type enforcement. This is the genuine vulnerability.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: missing-guardrail (plan-level set_fields_json bypasses Pydantic validation; task-level is already correctly validated)\\n\\nRoot-Cause Analysis:\\n1. Task-level updates route through `_validated_task_patch` \u2192 `Task.model_validate` \u2014 type-safe\\n2. Plan-level updates route through `cast()` \u2192 `backend.update_plan_fields` \u2014 no schema validation\\n3. There is no `Plan.model_validate` call on the plan-level patch path\\n4. `cast()` was used as a shortcut for type checking, masking the absent runtime validation\\n5. The issue description misattributed the risk as a coercion bug rather than a validation gap\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py:556\u2013564` \u2014 plan-level update path (uses `cast()`, no Pydantic validation)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py:483\u2013507` \u2014 `_validated_task_patch` (correct pattern to replicate for plan-level)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 `Plan` model (source for validation schema)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPlan-level field updates accept values of any type without schema validation. Integer fields passed as strings are written to YAML without error. Task-level updates are not affected \u2014 they are already validated through Pydantic. Severity: medium (only plan-level fields affected; task fields are protected).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNone \u2014 fix is self-contained within `server.py`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Plan-level `set_fields_json` values are validated against the `Plan` Pydantic model before being written (equivalent to the `_validated_task_patch` pattern used for task-level updates)\\n- [ ] A `_validated_plan_patch` helper (parallel to `_validated_task_patch`) is introduced using `Plan.model_validate`, not `cast()` or `Any`\\n- [ ] Passing a string value for an integer plan field raises `pydantic.ValidationError` rather than silently accepting it\\n- [ ] No use of `cast()` or `Any` as a substitute for runtime type validation in the update paths\\n- [ ] A test covers plan-level integer field rejection when a string is passed\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEstimate: S\\nReasoning: Introduce `_validated_plan_patch` mirroring `_validated_task_patch`, replace `cast()` call at line 563, add one test. No schema changes required.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n```python\\n# Task-level: SAFE \u2014 Pydantic validates and coerces\\nsam_update(\\\"P1/T1\\\", set_fields_json='{\\\"priority\\\": \\\"not-a-number\\\"}')\\n# \u2192 raises pydantic.ValidationError (priority must be int)\\n\\n# Plan-level: UNSAFE \u2014 no validation, wrong types accepted silently\\nsam_update(\\\"P1\\\", set_fields_json='{\\\"some-int-field\\\": \\\"should-be-int\\\"}')\\n# \u2192 accepted and written without type checking\\n```\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **sam_update coerces all set_fields_json values to str \u2014 integer fields broken** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: QG T1 code review of P912 \u2014 follow-up plan P1427\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d65ce65b0fbec21f8d9e74d191b56a78065b943da4550deb6f73a9f39ff8f618\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCuitA\"}"}